משה

 Multiple

 Moshe (משה) — the great cluster of Moshe's gematria and acronym connections:

 (1) Tziroof The letters of Moshe = ש׳ מה — "the Shin of Mah" [the 300 of the letter Shin + the Name Mah (45)];

 (2) Gematria Moshe (345) = gematria of חרון אף (charon af, "burning anger") [cross-reference from Section 8] — Moshe stands in the breach of divine anger;

 (3) Moshe (345) = gematria of שילה (Shiloh — the Divine Name and place associated with Yosef's descendants);

(4) Moshe (345) = gematria of שכה (a name/word in the source = 325... see source for precise value);

 (5) Moshe stands numerically between שמד (shemad, "destruction / forced apostasy" = 344) and רצון (ratzon, "will / favor" = 346) — Moshe mediates between the extremes of destruction and divine will;

 (6) Moshe Rabbeinu (משה רבינו, "Moshe our Teacher") = gematria of תרי"ג (613 — the number of commandments). Moshe our Teacher = the 613 commandments;

 (7–10) Roshay Saveivos Moshe appears as the first letters of four different phrases:

— מ׳ה ש׳היה ה׳וא: "That which was, it is" [Ecclesiastes 1:9];

 — מ׳חלוקת ש׳מאי ה׳לל: "the dispute of Shammai and Hillel";

 — מ׳ט"ט ש׳ר ה׳פנים: "Metatron, Prince of the Face";

 — מ׳תוקה ש׳נת ה׳עובד: "Sweet is the sleep of the laborer" [Ecclesiastes 5:11].
 [Moshe is the mediator of all opposites: between destruction and favor; between the eternal past and the eternal present; between the highest angelic prince and the sweetest sleep of the common laborer. His name contains multitudes.]


 Likutay Mooharan 4:9; 215; 6:7; 9:4; 13:3; 36:2; 56:8; 58:2; II:79; II:5:15

aligned_segments.en:
Malapoum (מלאפום — the vowel cholam when written as a Vov) = מלא פום (mala pum, Aramaic: "fills the mouth") — the vowel that fills and rounds the mouth with its sound. It corresponds to the Yud-Vov letter-pair [cross-reference from Section 10]. Likutay Mooharan 8:9; 34:5

 מלאך

 Multiple

 Malach (מלאך, "angel") yields three connections:

 (1) Tziroof Its letters are a permutation of כְּלָאֵם (kela'am, "He restrained them") [cross-reference from Section 11];

 (2) Gematria Malach = gematria of סוכה (sukkah, "the festival booth" = 91);

